#!/usr/bin/python3
"""Post a short changelog of lab work to Discord.

Managed by Ansible (roles/cmd_center/tasks/changelog.yml). Local edits are
overwritten.

Usage:
    lab-changelog daily [--dry-run] [--since ISO8601] [--no-llm]
    lab-changelog session-end [--dry-run] [--no-llm]

daily        Window starts one hour before the end of the last successful
             daily run (24 hours back on the first run, never more than 7
             days back) and ends now. --since overrides the start. Run by
             lab-changelog.timer.
session-end  Claude Code SessionEnd hook. Reads the hook JSON on stdin, detaches
             the real work and returns at once. It always exits 0 and never
             writes to stdout, so it can never break or slow a session exit.
--dry-run    Print the Discord payload(s) as JSON. Posts nothing, fetches no
             secret and records nothing.

Facts come from GitHub (gh), never from a session transcript. The transcript
is only opened to read the timestamp of its first entry.

SECURITY: the repos are public, so PR and issue titles and bodies are
untrusted. Every piece of text that reaches Discord goes through
discord_text(), every payload carries allowed_mentions {"parse": []}, link
targets are rebuilt from the validated repo name and number instead of taken
from GitHub's response, and the webhook URL is never logged or put in an
exception.

Configuration (environment, all optional):
    LAB_CHANGELOG_REPOS             comma separated owner/name list
    LAB_CHANGELOG_OP_REFERENCE      1Password reference of the webhook URL
    LAB_CHANGELOG_OP_LIB_DIR        directory holding op-killswitch.sh and
                                    op-secret-cache.sh
    LAB_CHANGELOG_OP_TOKEN_FILE     1Password service account token file
    LAB_CHANGELOG_SESSION_MIN_SECS  minimum session length to post (600)
    LAB_CHANGELOG_STATE_DIR         state, lock and log directory
    LAB_CHANGELOG_CLAUDE_BIN        claude CLI path ("" disables highlights)
    LAB_CHANGELOG_CLAUDE_MODEL      model alias for highlights (haiku)
    LAB_CHANGELOG_CLAUDE_TIMEOUT    highlight generation timeout in seconds (90)
    LAB_CHANGELOG_HOST              host name shown in the title
    LAB_CHANGELOG_CONFIG            KEY=VALUE file holding any of the above
                                    (/etc/default/lab-changelog); the
                                    environment wins over the file
"""

